This patch fixes the GridLayout width calculation issue.

The problem: containerWidth is being set to a very small value (~100px) instead of the actual canvas width.

Root cause: The canvas ref measurement happens before the CSS has finished calculating the actual width.

Solution: Use a more robust width calculation with multiple fallbacks and delayed measurement.

Apply this fix to DesignCanvas.js:

1. Change the initial containerWidth from 1200 to a calculated value based on window
2. Add multiple measurement attempts
3. Use requestAnimationFrame for proper timing

Replace the width calculation useEffect with this:

```javascript
// Calculate container width dynamically and handle window resize
useEffect(() => {
  let mounted = true;

  const updateWidth = () => {
    if (!mounted) return;

    if (canvasRef.current) {
      // Get the actual rendered width
      const rect = canvasRef.current.getBoundingClientRect();
      const width = rect.width || canvasRef.current.offsetWidth || canvasRef.current.clientWidth;

      console.log('DesignCanvas width measurement:', {
        'getBoundingClientRect': rect.width,
        'offsetWidth': canvasRef.current.offsetWidth,
        'clientWidth': canvasRef.current.clientWidth,
        'selected': width
      });

      // Account for padding (24px on each side = 48px total)
      const adjustedWidth = Math.max(width - 48, 800); // Minimum 800px

      if (adjustedWidth !== containerWidth) {
        console.log(`Updating containerWidth from ${containerWidth} to ${adjustedWidth}`);
        setContainerWidth(adjustedWidth);
      }
    } else {
      console.log('DesignCanvas: canvasRef.current is null');
      // Fallback to window-based calculation
      const fallbackWidth = Math.min(window.innerWidth - 400, 1200); // Account for sidebars
      if (fallbackWidth !== containerWidth) {
        setContainerWidth(fallbackWidth);
      }
    }
  };

  // Multiple measurement attempts
  const measure = () => {
    updateWidth();

    // Try again after a frame to ensure CSS has loaded
    requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      if (mounted) updateWidth();
    });

    // One more try after a short delay
    setTimeout(() => {
      if (mounted) updateWidth();
    }, 100);
  };

  // Initial measurement
  measure();

  // Update on window resize
  window.addEventListener('resize', updateWidth);

  return () => {
    mounted = false;
    window.removeEventListener('resize', updateWidth);
  };
}, [containerWidth]); // Include containerWidth as dependency
```

This should fix the width calculation issue.
